WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.560
A wrangle doesn't have much of a backstory.

00:00:04.860 --> 00:00:08.500
It's a vaguely Soviet, post-apocalyptic,

00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:13.800
dystopian, abandoned hellhole, full of guns and homes to loot.

00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:18.700
And you and 99 strangers are jumping off of a burning plane right into it.

00:00:20.600 --> 00:00:27.300
Your parachute will ensure the fall doesn't kill you, but once you're down there. It's you against the island.

00:00:32.440 --> 00:00:36.120
99 strangers are on the hunt for you and each other.

00:00:36.120 --> 00:00:39.420
Every single one of them wants to be the last one standing.

00:00:39.429 --> 00:00:41.519
Every single one of them wants to win.

00:00:42.040 --> 00:00:44.940
They loot homes as soon as they land.

00:00:44.960 --> 00:00:50.080
Hunting for weapons and armor scrounging the map to find anything that could be of use.

00:00:50.080 --> 00:00:55.740
Looking down your sights as you open the door and a guy with a shotgun blasts you in the face.

00:00:57.540 --> 00:01:00.840
People have always wanted a Battle Royale video game.

00:01:01.020 --> 00:01:03.020
But it never happened.

00:01:03.020 --> 00:01:06.960
First came the original team deathmatch island Battle Royale.

00:01:06.960 --> 00:01:12.700
The Japanese book and movie told the story of 42 students dropped on a deserted island,

00:01:12.700 --> 00:01:15.780
and forced to kill each other until only one was left.

00:01:25.869 --> 00:01:30.148
It got people asking, What they would do if they were in that situation?

00:01:30.360 --> 00:01:36.760
But the movie was not released in the West for years; leaving it an obscure cult classic.

00:01:36.780 --> 00:01:42.380
Then years later, Hunger Games came around, and it re-ignited the fire.

00:01:42.380 --> 00:01:44.400
People wanted Battle Royale games.

00:01:44.590 --> 00:01:49.769
But no one was making them, but one person wanted it more than anybody else.

00:01:50.440 --> 00:01:52.440
Brenden "Player Unknown" Green.

00:01:53.019 --> 00:01:55.289
Brendon green was not a game designer.

00:01:55.380 --> 00:02:00.740
He was an Irish photographer and web designer who followed the love of his life to Brazil.

00:02:00.740 --> 00:02:04.940
Two years later, he was divorced and looking to get his life back on track.

00:02:04.940 --> 00:02:06.740
He made it back home to Ireland.

00:02:06.740 --> 00:02:11.860
And while living on welfare, Greene discovered the games ARMA and DayZ.

00:02:11.860 --> 00:02:16.080
For those who don't know ARMA is a hyper-realistic military shooter.

00:02:16.080 --> 00:02:20.660
Known for the scale of its combat, its attention to detail, and graphic fidelity.

00:02:20.820 --> 00:02:25.240
Also known for being the foundation for an incredible number of mods.

00:02:25.240 --> 00:02:28.140
Many of which were spun off of into their own games.

00:02:28.140 --> 00:02:30.960
DayZ is one of the best-known ARMA mods.

00:02:31.040 --> 00:02:35.900
Which use the hyper-realistic combat mechanics to simulate a zombie apocalypse.

00:02:36.200 --> 00:02:39.620
So yeah, I started off making a mod basically back in ARMA2.

00:02:40.020 --> 00:02:42.120
Because I want to make a game I wanted to play.

00:02:42.120 --> 00:02:45.400
I saw games like the survivor games which were events for streamers.

00:02:45.400 --> 00:02:52.100
I wanted to play that myself so I decided to see if I could actually make one, and ARMA 2: Battle Royale was born.

00:02:52.100 --> 00:03:00.420
The Battle Royale mod for ARMA 2 was a departure from the tightly directed experiences offered by Triple A games like Assassin's Creed.

00:03:00.420 --> 00:03:03.080
Green was not interested in those types of games.

00:03:03.390 --> 00:03:06.559
He wanted something looser, something grittier.

00:03:06.560 --> 00:03:11.220
Something that gave you the freedom to show what you would do in a battle to the death.

00:03:11.380 --> 00:03:15.600
As DayZ broke free of ARMA and became a standalone game.

00:03:15.600 --> 00:03:20.460
Other developers took notice of how popular Green's mods were in the niche ARMA community.

00:03:20.760 --> 00:03:22.590
Sony Online Entertainment.

00:03:22.590 --> 00:03:29.570
Now known as DayBreak, hired Greene as a consultant on their own Dayz style zombie survival game.

00:03:29.960 --> 00:03:34.120
That mode eventually became H1Z1 King of the Kill.

00:03:34.160 --> 00:03:37.500
But by February 2016, Green had moved on.

00:03:37.500 --> 00:03:40.720
He was headed to Korea where he got an interesting offer.

00:03:41.040 --> 00:03:47.480
Chang Han Kim, a Korean game designer working for Blue Hole wanted to make a Battle Royale game.

00:03:47.540 --> 00:03:52.540
He was inspired by DayZ, but when he researched the Battle Royale format more and more.

00:03:52.580 --> 00:03:55.060
He kept coming cross Green.

00:03:55.060 --> 00:03:59.300
And less than one month later, he was Blue Holes creative director.

00:03:59.300 --> 00:04:00.960
Development moved fast.

00:04:00.960 --> 00:04:05.800
Green and Kim's team had the autonomy to create the game that they wanted.

00:04:05.800 --> 00:04:08.120
And they wanted it to be playable within one year.

00:04:12.160 --> 00:04:15.060
The game started its development in early 2016.

00:04:15.670 --> 00:04:18.640
And the plan was to follow an early access schedule.

00:04:19.010 --> 00:04:25.839
Green and Kim wanted to get the game in customers hands fast for a low cost and keep improving it over time.

00:04:26.240 --> 00:04:29.590
But the foundation needed to be laid down before anything else.

00:04:40.460 --> 00:04:46.450
The team made a small game, one map, one mode, a handful of weapons were added after the launch.

00:04:46.540 --> 00:04:54.620
But from the day it was released on early access in March 2017 to today, Battlegrounds has been the same game.

00:04:55.000 --> 00:04:59.260
However, when it first came out there wasn't quite anything like it.

00:04:59.260 --> 00:05:01.520
Sure Green's mods were still out there.

00:05:01.540 --> 00:05:05.520
But mods are never quite as popular as standalone games.

00:05:06.040 --> 00:05:11.640
Battlegrounds was a breath of fresh air amidst the high budget lavishly produced shooters on the market.

00:05:11.640 --> 00:05:13.060
It was messy.

00:05:14.380 --> 00:05:16.380
It was tense.

00:05:33.780 --> 00:05:35.400
And it was complicated.

00:05:35.400 --> 00:05:37.880
But most importantly it was fun.

00:05:37.880 --> 00:05:40.420
The island is the most important part too.

00:05:40.420 --> 00:05:43.980
While Green has said that his team is working on more maps.

00:05:43.980 --> 00:05:48.260
A wrangle will always be the most iconic thing about Battlegrounds.

00:05:48.260 --> 00:05:55.160
It's the game's main character with familiar landmarks, wide open spaces, and bizarre unique topography

00:05:55.810 --> 00:05:57.610
It's not realistic.

00:05:57.610 --> 00:06:06.060
Swamps, farmland, mountains, and towns all mingle together to make a backdrop that has much of a hand in the action as the players do.

00:06:06.060 --> 00:06:08.640
And the players came to battlegrounds fast.

00:06:08.860 --> 00:06:13.300
For only $20, they got to live the fantasy of surviving the apocalypse.

00:06:13.300 --> 00:06:15.860
The games player base grew every week.

00:06:16.080 --> 00:06:21.200
10 million rounds of battlegrounds were played in the game's first four months.

00:06:21.200 --> 00:06:23.960
And it made eleven million dollars in three days.

00:06:24.100 --> 00:06:27.200
By April it had sold a million copies.

00:06:27.280 --> 00:06:28.320
One month later.

00:06:28.320 --> 00:06:32.660
It was at 2 million, the next month it hit 4 million.

00:06:32.660 --> 00:06:37.860
In August, Battlegrounds became the most played game on Steam in terms of concurrent players.

00:06:37.860 --> 00:06:43.740
By September, it had beaten Dota 2's record of 1.29 million concurrent players

00:06:43.740 --> 00:06:47.580
By October it had hit 2 million players on Steam.

00:06:47.580 --> 00:06:51.420
And became the most popular game in South Korean PC bangs.

00:06:51.520 --> 00:06:54.160
Beating long-time king, League of Legends.

00:06:54.680 --> 00:07:00.620
When the game cracked 2 million copies sold, Blue Hole held a charity Invitational tournament.

00:07:05.060 --> 00:07:12.200
Three months later ESL held the first major battlegrounds tournament cementing a possible eSports future for the game.

00:07:12.560 --> 00:07:19.600
Green told gamesindustry. biz that he has always envisioned his mods to be a spectator sport someday.

00:07:19.600 --> 00:07:22.680
And his baby was finally taking its first steps.

00:07:22.900 --> 00:07:28.140
People still ask if battlegrounds can be an eSport it has the audience and the player base.

00:07:28.189 --> 00:07:30.518
The only problem is the logistics.

00:07:30.980 --> 00:07:35.880
Gathering 100 people for a LAN tournament is not the easiest thing in the world.

00:07:35.880 --> 00:07:39.840
Which might limit it to events like ESL Ones and Dreamhacks.

00:07:39.840 --> 00:07:43.520
But eSports is not the only place Battlegrounds is growing.

00:07:43.520 --> 00:07:48.680
The game is selling more and more copies by the day and even bigger companies are taking notice.

00:07:48.949 --> 00:07:51.609
Tencent made a deal to publish the game in China.

00:07:52.000 --> 00:07:54.480
Facebook cut a streaming deal with Blue Hole.

00:07:54.540 --> 00:07:58.360
Epic Games who assisted in modifying the Unreal Engine for Battlegrounds.

00:07:58.360 --> 00:08:02.600
Made a battlegrounds inspired play mode for their game Fortnite.

00:08:02.600 --> 00:08:09.220
And Microsoft touted a timed console exclusive version of battlegrounds for Xbox one at E3 2017.

00:08:09.220 --> 00:08:15.720
We can't wait to bring Playerunkown's Battlegrounds exclusively to Xbox One later this year.

00:08:15.720 --> 00:08:21.140
With an update for Xbox One X enhancements shipping with the final version.

00:08:21.440 --> 00:08:23.029
Battlegrounds future is bright.

00:08:23.029 --> 00:08:26.720
There's no sign that the game will stop growing anytime soon.

00:08:26.720 --> 00:08:28.840
And with imitators starting to crop up.

00:08:28.840 --> 00:08:33.440
That just gives  Battlegrounds more chances to innovate and be better than the competition.

00:08:33.980 --> 00:08:38.700
Battlegrounds is the beginning of a new video genre and no one saw it coming.

00:08:41.860 --> 00:08:46.440
Thanks for watching if you want more great content be sure to hit that subscribe button.

